{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/842218-how-to-kill-a-wraith-or-a-spectre","id":842218,"title":"How to Kill a Wraith or a Spectre?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Wraith: The Oblivion"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-04T16:12:55-08:00","id":842218,"title":"How to Kill a Wraith or a Spectre?","content":"Every time a Wraith's corpus goes to zero, he pay a visit to the Labyrinth and then he's back, maybe a bit more crazy than before, but still &quot;alive&quot;. I find this cycle a bit boring, it reminds me digimons wich turns into eggs again when they &quot;die&quot;. There's no way to permanently destroy a Wraith?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-04T16:44:28-08:00","id":842238,"title":"","content":"Spectres don't go into Destruction Harrowings if they lose their last point of corpus. They meet Oblivion for good.<br /> <br /> Wraiths, alas, are hardy bastards and will keep coming back until they lose every dot of permanent corpus. You can just soulforge them, though, so it's not as if you can't permanently get rid of your enemies.<br /> <br /> Even Samuel Haight isn't coming back from being soulforged. He'll be an ashtray forever.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-06T08:22:17-08:00","id":842993,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new\">When Wraiths loses all of their Corpus levels, yes, they go into Harrowings. The thing is there's no solid guarantee that they're coming out of them. IIRC, they could end up as Spectres or they could plummet into Oblivion.<br /> <br /> The Digimon example: When the digimon dies, they can reform as an egg if they go through a deeply personal and emotional psychodrama and find some level of acceptance, peace, solace or acceptable loathing and not give into their semi-feral and nihilistic digi-shadows. Or by not totally giving into the despair of absolute cosmic entropy and getting sucked down the faucet of Nothing \u2122.<br /> <br /> What makes you think of Harrowings as boring? <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:8px\">((Also - what ABL said - Spectres are kinda one-trick cenobite ponies.)</span></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T05:20:56-08:00","id":843365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/842218-how-to-kill-a-wraith-or-a-spectre#post842218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Every time a Wraith's corpus goes to zero, he pay a visit to the Labyrinth and then he's back, maybe a bit more crazy than before, but still &quot;alive&quot;. I find this cycle a bit boring, it reminds me digimons wich turns into eggs again when they &quot;die&quot;. There's no way to permanently destroy a Wraith?</div> </div> </div> </div>If you are willing to make the trip and risk staggering amounts of danger, you can chuck a wraith into Oblivion itself. No one comes back from that. But seriously, that's a harder path and a waste of perfectly good soulforging materials.<br /> <br /> But really, the point is that 'death' has already happened, wraiths were tenacious enough to keep going anyway. It takes something massive to put one down for good. That or the sheer weight of inevitability that wears away at their half-souls and promises that even if they live thousands of years they will eventually be claimed, damned, or driven mad by Oblivion.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T23:54:32-08:00","id":843837,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/842218-how-to-kill-a-wraith-or-a-spectre?p=842238#post842238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spectres don't go into Destruction Harrowings if they lose their last point of corpus. They meet Oblivion for good.<br /> <br /> Wraiths, alas, are hardy bastards and will keep coming back until they lose every dot of permanent corpus. You can just soulforge them, though, so it's not as if you can't permanently get rid of your enemies.<br /> <br /> Even Samuel Haight isn't coming back from being soulforged. He'll be an ashtray forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't forget Stygian steel weaponry. Created by &quot;alloying&quot; a soul with bits of the Labyrinth, a Stygian steel weapon does aggravated damage to wraiths and Spectres. &quot;Killing&quot; a wraith with one drops them <i>immediately</i> into a Destruction Harrowing - fail that, and the wraith is permanently destroyed.<br /> <br /> Less lethal (but still very permanent), a wraith can be turned into a barghest. Lobotomized with Stygian steel, locked into a soulsteel mask, and doomed to hunt for his captors for all eternity . . . Not exactly a good fate","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4624-one-vorlon","name":"One Vorlon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"537"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T13:25:45-07:00","id":846707,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/842218-how-to-kill-a-wraith-or-a-spectre?p=842238#post842238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Samuel Haight isn't coming back from being soulforged. He'll be an ashtray forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>Silly question, I know, but what if you made a robot out of soulforged stuff? Or some other sort of object that could move on its own power, providing it had power.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T15:18:28-07:00","id":846738,"title":"","content":"Thank you for your help guys! Talking about arrowings a wraith is always aware about them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-13T17:52:35-07:00","id":846831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/842218-how-to-kill-a-wraith-or-a-spectre?p=846707#post846707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Silly question, I know, but what if you made a robot out of soulforged stuff? Or some other sort of object that could move on its own power, providing it had power.</div> </div> </div> </div>That robot wouldn't have the consciousness of any of the soulforged components because soulforging (allegedly) destroys consciousness.<br /> <br /> It's possible that a particularly powerful wraith or spectre soulforged into such a component might try to gain control of the robot it is a part of, but it'd have to be a pretty epic-level character. It's also not something ever stated in the rules; it's just something you can infer from the fluff.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T16:08:11-07:00","id":848462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/842218-how-to-kill-a-wraith-or-a-spectre?p=842238#post842238\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spectres don't go into Destruction Harrowings if they lose their last point of corpus. They meet Oblivion for good.<br /> <br /> Wraiths, alas, are hardy bastards and will keep coming back until they lose every dot of permanent corpus. You can just soulforge them, though, so it's not as if you can't permanently get rid of your enemies.<br /> <br /> Even Samuel Haight isn't coming back from being soulforged. He'll be an ashtray forever.</div> </div> </div> </div>or until the ashtray wears out... am curious... think that his fate was deliberate vindictiveness by the writing staff against him? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-16T16:39:22-07:00","id":848475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/842218-how-to-kill-a-wraith-or-a-spectre?p=848462#post848462\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> or until the ashtray wears out... am curious... think that his fate was deliberate vindictiveness by the writing staff against him? </div> </div> </div> </div>Oh absolutely. And an in-joke.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T13:06:15-07:00","id":849414,"title":"","content":"Didn't the WtA 20th edition have an adventure that threatened to return him to an active role in the World of Darkness? It seems, as with many subjects, that there is disagreement and a back-and-forth tug of war among the writers about Samuel Haight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-18T13:56:58-07:00","id":849440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/842218-how-to-kill-a-wraith-or-a-spectre?p=849414#post849414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Didn't the WtA 20th edition have an adventure that threatened to return him to an active role in the World of Darkness? It seems, as with many subjects, that there is disagreement and a back-and-forth tug of war among the writers about Samuel Haight.</div> </div> </div> </div>More a figurative return than anything else","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T04:14:19-07:00","id":852321,"title":"","content":"I've read somewhere on the web that if a wraith lose all his corpus due to aggravated damage, he's destroyed without undergo a Destruction Arrowing, Can you confirm it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T08:54:49-07:00","id":852445,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">As of Second Edition, that is incorrect.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:courier new, courier, monospace\">&quot;If a wraith loses all of his remaining Corpus Levels due to aggravated damage, he immediately tumbles into the Labyrinth and undergoes a Destructive Harrowing,&quot; (Wraith: the Oblivion Second Edition, p. 233).</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:8px\"><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">&lt;signature&gt; something witty &lt;/signature&gt;</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/302-nazfool","name":"Nazfool","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar302_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"753"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-24T10:25:22-07:00","id":852470,"title":"","content":"Hmm maybe it was an outdated info...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2457-ipergigio","name":"Ipergigio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2457_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-18T08:00:40-07:00","id":1105081,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ipergigio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/wraith-the-oblivion/842218-how-to-kill-a-wraith-or-a-spectre?p=852470#post852470\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm maybe it was an outdated info...</div> </div> </div> </div>Ipergigio - I believe I know where you got the info. Page 58 of The Sea of Shadows:<br /> <br /> &quot;If all or most of the damage was normal (i.e., not aggravated), the above holds true. If a wraith loses all her corpus due to aggravated damage, there is no Harrowing; the wraith is dead forever. Aggravated damage is caused by a power of Moliate, when the wraith is Embodied, or by Stygian of darksteel weapons.&quot;<br /> <br /> But, per Nazfool, I'd go with whatever second edition says. That is until Wr20 comes out <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13564-trategos_sol","name":"Trategos_Sol","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13564_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"89"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}